      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "COSMIC CHARGER (1) was out of the money when resuming from a spell last start over 1200m at Pakenham Synthetic, but was hard to miss, hitting the line stylishly to be beaten 2.25 lengths. Better for that, this is no tougher and more suited this trip. PICK A SYMPHONY (4) was allowed to drift back from an outside draw last time but found the line strongly to finish fourth, beaten 3.5 lengths, over 1400m at Mildura. Sure to be tough to hold out now at peak fitness from the inside alley. TRUE PROPHET (6) finished seventh two runs back then improved last start when he worked home well but found a couple better over 1300m at Seymour, beaten 2.5 lengths. Finds a suitable assignment and can find winning form. TORN (2) has placed at two of three runs on the home track and will find this a touch easier than last start. I'M DYNAMITE (7) is another who is in a more suitable contest this time and draws to get his chance.",
